<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caernarfon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caernarfon is a royal town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menai-strait">Menai Strait</a> in Gwynedd, north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. It grew beside the Roman fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segontium">Segontium</a>, and after the conquest of Wales Edward I built Caernarfon Castle there from 1283 as the seat of English government in North Wales. The castle, part of a World Heritage Site, saw the investitures of the princes of Wales in 1911 and 1969.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caernarfon.jpg" alt="Caernarfon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AJ Marshall · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caernarfon_Castle_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
